comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T21:28:17.876Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented: when an item_store_write override transforms contents, redirects the path or skips the write (or an item_store_delete override skips or redirects the removal), mutateItem/deleteItem re-locate and parse the stored item under the still-held lock and advance the revision scope to that hash (readOverriddenCommitRevision in core/store/item-store.ts). A missing item advances to the empty tombstone; an unlocatable or unparseable one advances to an unmatchable revision (fail closed). Unoverridden writes keep the in-memory afterDocument, so ordinary writes pay no extra IO. advanceItemMutationPreconditions takes an optional revision. Negative control: the five new specs in tests/unit/core/store/item-store.spec.ts all fail against the pre-fix item-store.ts and pass with it."
